data module_storage_supply_dissolution_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "dissolve-on: host-effect emission (witness-realization lane). The host handler for module_storage_bindings_for_source_roots is hand-written Rust at the effect boundary TODAY; when host-effect emission lands, the producer is EMITTED from this .dag model instead, and the hand handler retires. Declared here rather than left implicit so the scaffold cannot linger unmarked (§6: every scaffold lands with a named dissolution trigger). Until then the consistency witness is what keeps the handler honest to this interface, in two enrolled halves: the LIVE half (v2.test.long.module_binding_host_consistency, on the module-binding supply gate's wet cadence) asserts host-emitted rows == module_storage_bindings_from_ingest over the same sources, and the DISCRIMINATING half (v2.test.claim.module_storage_binding, per-PR fast lane, zero parse cost) pins the comparator itself with perturbed rows — module_storage_agreement_reports_divergent_on_wrong_module and module_storage_agreement_reports_uncovered_on_missing_row both go RED if module_storage_host_agrees_with_oracle ever regresses to answering ModuleStorageAgrees unconditionally, which is the exact way the live half would go vacuously green (review 39735).")



